cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use seqcounter, please cite it as below, together with BBTools."
title: "seqcounter: count the occurrences of reference sequences in sequencing reads or genome assemblies"
type: software
abstract: >-
  seqcounter counts how many sequencing reads (fastq) or contigs (fasta) contain each sequence of a reference fasta
  file, using Seal from BBTools. Matches are counted on both strands and with mismatches, single-end reads,
  paired-end reads and assemblies are all supported, and a folder of samples gives one table of counts per
  reference sequence and per sample, with a per-sample summary of how much was read and matched, and a JSON report
  of the run.
authors:
  - family-names: Duceppe
    given-names: Marc-Olivier
    email: marc-olivier.duceppe@inspection.gc.ca
    affiliation: Canadian Food Inspection Agency
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-30"
# The Zenodo DOI of the archived release is added here once the release is published.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/duceppemo/seqcounter"
url: "https://github.com/duceppemo/seqcounter/wiki"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - k-mer counting
  - reference sequences
  - sequencing reads
  - genome assemblies
references:
